+### Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-6B4EFF)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=transitive-bullshit%2Fnextjs-notion-starter-kit)
+
+Wasmer detects Next.js, runs the project's `build` script (`pnpm run build`, which fetches your public Notion pages) and serves the production build with Node.
+
+The button builds this public repository as-is; it does not fork or copy it into your GitHub account. To point the site at your own Notion page via `rootNotionPageId` in [site.config.ts](./site.config.ts) and redeploy on every push, fork the repo and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard.
+
+No environment variables are required. `NEXT_PUBLIC_FATHOM_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_ID` and the Redis variables (`REDIS_HOST`, `REDIS_PASSWORD`, see [Redis](#redis)) are optional and can be added in the app's Settings → Environment Vars.
+
 ## URL Paths
 
 The app defaults to slightly different URL paths in dev vs prod (though pasting any dev pathname into prod will work and vice-versa).
